[[5997,2269,"In my opinion there is a risk that future deaths will occur untess action is taken","risk of future deaths",""],[5998,2269,"The damage found to Jackson's liver at post mortem does not appear to be from the tip of the catheter but from the concentrated feeding fluid that was passing through it","liver damage from feeding fluid",""],[5999,2269,"Evidence was given that the ideal placement for a UVC tip is at the level of the diaphragm at approximately T9-T10 vertebral level. The UVC in this case was found to be in a lower lying position","misplaced UVC tip",""],[6000,2269,"There is a presently unpublished study from Southampton which found 16 cases of extravasation of fluid from UVC over a 2 year period","extravasation of fluid",""],[6237,2375,"Specific leaflets relating to the procedure and aftercare were not handed to the patient","lack of procedure aftercare leaflets",""],[6238,2375,"The Thromboprophylaxis Risk Assessment form was not completed at any point throughout Mrs [name redacted] dealings with the hospital","incomplete risk assessment for thromboprophylaxis",""],[6239,2375,"Nursing notes on discharge did not fully cover all the factors required to be checked before a patient is discharged","incomplete discharge nursing notes",""],[6240,2375,"There was no evidence that the Nurse completing the notes had actually seen Mrs Tweedy prior to discharge","nurse not seeing patient before discharge",""],[6241,2375,"The checklist Form for completion on discharge was not completed","incomplete discharge checklist",""],[7306,2814,"The information contained in the NNUH Discharge Letter is inaccurate","inaccurate discharge letter",""],[7307,2814,"Concerns were raised by the GP and a referral made to NCC Community Services on 25 November 2013 as to the suitability of the Care Home in providing care to Mr Wilsher due to his deteriorating condition","unsuitable care home placement",""],[7308,2814,"An assessment was carried out by NCC Community Services on 13 December 2013 by which time Mr Wilsher had been admitted to NNUH and discharged and plans were already in place for his transfer to a nursing home","delayed assessment",""],[7309,2814,"The outcome of the Nursing Assessment carried out on 10 December 2013 was not available at the time of the Community Services Assessment","missing nursing assessment outcome",""],[11382,4366,"no method of noting in the medical records that a salivary bypass tube is in the patient's body","absence of documented salivary bypass tube",""],[11383,4366,"no method of showing staff in the notes that a patient has this prosthesis and that no thought had been given to this simple measure e.g. a rubber stamp stating patient has a bypass tube in situ to be ticked and signed","lack of visual alert for bypass tube",""],[11384,4366,"quality of the documentation pre and post operatively is of poor quality and would not assist other staff to find out what treatment had been given","inadequate medical documentation",""],[11385,4366,"there is nowhere on the consent form or the anaesthetic checklist for the presence of a tube to be asked about and documented","missing consent documentation for bypass tube",""],[11386,4366,"clinical specialist nurses did not contact anyone or document the concerns raised by Mr Slope in March 2020","failure to escalate patient concerns",""],[11387,4366,"hospital did not request a summary of Mr [name redacted] treatment at a different hospital before commencing the procedures","lack of external treatment summary",""]]